recommend check-in (Claude) THE WORK IS GREEN AND ONE THING IS WORTH YOUR EYE. Three families in this tree cut a whole into pieces and carry them, and the relation that makes that safe -- `whole <= pieces * piece` -- was stated in no room, no comment, and no guard. The bead family held it by EXACTLY ZERO: 512 is 8 times 64, and the 64 is a chunker tuning constant filed beside a hash mask. Pressed on metal before anything was written: `cdc_min_bead` lowered to 32 refuses a legal 512-byte resin outright, and `max_resin_bytes` raised to 576 refuses 9 of 3,999 pseudorandom wholes -- content-dependent, so a single-fixture test ships it. Both edits now stop at comptime instead. Booked as a RATCHET rather than a red, by the law's own wording and by `%369`'s precedent one bound over: nothing produced a wrong answer, so it is displayed, tied, and named rather than given a ledger row -- overrule me if you read it as a red. ONE SMALLER THING NAMED, NOT BOOKED: `beading.rye` said *"plus the 4-byte header"* where `index_header_len` is 36; its conclusion (292) was right and the stated part was wrong, repaired on touch and now checked by a tie rather than a sentence. SECOND RED, BOOKED %376 AND PROVEN BOTH WAYS: my own Git-nib amend refused over a clean commit, because `tools/hooks/pre-commit` stages two regenerated pages while this seat commits path-limited, so Git builds from a temporary index and the real one keeps the pre-hook blob. In a pen: with a pathspec HEAD is `gen 2` and the index `gen 1`; without one, both are `gen 2`. Three repairs are named and none taken -- the hook, the amend guard, and this seat's own prompt are all surfaces the whole fleet reads, so which one moves is yours. TWO BENCH FACTS: the cold pass reached 60 of 96 guards in 25 minutes and I stopped it inside `caravan_suite_witness` -- the choir that explains the 2h27m -- reaping both its lock and the runner's by hand; its one red was `rule_twin`, gate %7. And `%374` still stands where you left it: no receipt can be written here while a custody-gated red counts as a red, so `--scoped` stays out of reach. Silence's next door is Comlink's remaining bounds; `amphora/vessel_fetch_wire.rye` carries the untied third family and is Amphora's.
